<title>USA: U.S. February trade gap narrows on stronger exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. February trade gap narrows on stronger exports.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cheaper oil and a surge in aircraft exports to Britain during February helped shrink the U.S. trade gap by 8.5 percent to $11.59 billion, the Commerce Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Total exports rose 4 percent from January to a record $73.46 billion, nearly double the 2.1 percent pickup in monthly imports, which also hit a record $85.05 billion in February.</p>
</text>
